    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίπτομαι</span></b> , pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέλιμμαι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be eager</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε μεῖον οὔτ᾽ ἴσον λελιμμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					355
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): c. gen., <i>to be eager for, long for</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχης λελιμμένος</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				380
			</span></i>:—later in 
				Act.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίπτω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.813
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				131
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				126
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίψ: ἐπιθυμία</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλιπεν,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιθυμητικῶς ἤσθιεν</span>
			, Id., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιψουρία</span>, and perh.
			Lith. <i>li[etilde]pti</i> 'command'.)</div>
